                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "310df26e-ffec-3b23-bf54-d03570476a57",
                        "entry_id": "de6400f3-af46-33a5-bf1c-da48337ff494",
                        "glosses": [
                            "cytrynowożółty barwnik azowy używany głównie do celów spożywczych"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d1e6e95-7ff7-45e2-9392-dc32df658986",
                                "sense_id": "310df26e-ffec-3b23-bf54-d03570476a57",
                                "text": "Liczne zastrzeżenia budzą również niektóre syntetyczne barwniki, szczególnie azowe i nieazowe, w tym głównie tartrazyna, która jest szkodliwa dla astmatyków i alergików, a zwłaszcza dla uczulonych na aspirynę"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cbd8a51d-597a-4c50-be71-dad0c702d0b2",
                        "source_entry_id": "de6400f3-af46-33a5-bf1c-da48337ff494",
                        "source_sense_id": "310df26e-ffec-3b23-bf54-d03570476a57",
                        "target_lang_word": "tartrazine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tartrazine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "303c8b43-74b9-348c-a5c3-2b58e2c3a7d9",
                                        "entry_id": "11d308b8-9680-3e39-af56-8dd06853c85c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lemon-yellow azo dye used as a food colouring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bd6f877-3374-4dab-9c1b-a0c8c1102bda",
                                                "sense_id": "303c8b43-74b9-348c-a5c3-2b58e2c3a7d9",
                                                "text": "Rowlands and Gorecki said that existing methods to turn tissue transparent use solutions that have side effects such as dehydration and swelling and can alter the structure of the tissue. However, tartrazine was used at a low concentration, and its effects were easily undone, potentially facilitating prolonged study of biological processes in live animals, they wrote."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecd4bcbd-fd9f-40e1-a071-531cfbe8013e",
                                                "sense_id": "303c8b43-74b9-348c-a5c3-2b58e2c3a7d9",
                                                "text": "The European Union requires a warning label on products that contain three artificial food dyes approved in the U.S.:\nYellow No. 5, also known as tartrazine.\nRed No. 40, also called E129 or Allura Red AC.\nYellow No. 6, called sunset yellow or E110."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "becc1b40-c686-46a4-8f1d-0429ec57ceca",
                        "source_entry_id": "de6400f3-af46-33a5-bf1c-da48337ff494",
                        "source_sense_id": "310df26e-ffec-3b23-bf54-d03570476a57",
                        "target_lang_word": "tartrazine",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tartrazine",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98fb101b-af55-3981-91bb-f9f6703df29d",
                                        "entry_id": "f375a5dc-ce3f-3528-91cd-fea6167534bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Composé chimique de formule brute C₁₆H₉N₄Na₃O₉S₂, utilisé comme colorant alimentaire jaune, et aussi pour teinter la laine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f9488da-fe7b-4bb8-8e24-7839f3c65906",
                                                "sense_id": "98fb101b-af55-3981-91bb-f9f6703df29d",
                                                "text": "Du moins jusqu’à aujourd’hui : des chercheurs ont réussi à rendre transparente la peau de souris en les badigeonnant d’un simple colorant alimentaire, la tartrazine, couramment utilisé par l’industrie pour doter des sodas ou des chips d’une belle teinte rouge orangée."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
